meta {
  name: Update User
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "first_name": "Updated",
    "middle_name": "",
    "last_name": "Name",
    "email": "updated@example.com",
    "mobile": "9876543210",
    "role_name": "senior_sales_executive",
    "manager_id": null,
    "is_active": true,
    "force_password_change": false,
    "send_email_notification": true
  }
}

docs {
  send_email_notification (optional, default true): only acted on when this PATCH
  actually changes the user's branch access or home branch (a plain profile edit
  sends nothing). When true AND the acting admin holds admin.team.notify (or rank
  >= org_admin), the user is emailed which branches were added/removed and the
  new home branch. Set false to skip.

  email, when supplied, is normalized to lowercase and trimmed before it is
  stored (schema 1.48.0) -- the same rule as create. Editing a user's email to a
  mixed-case value lands the canonical spelling; the database refuses anything
  else (chk_users_email_lowercase).
}
